Here's a complete implementation of a reusable Angular dropdown component with TypeScript, HTML, and CSS:

### 1. Component Implementation (`dropdown.component.ts`)
```typescript
import { Component, Input, Output, EventEmitter, ElementRef, ViewChild, HostListener } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-dropdown',
  templateUrl: './dropdown.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./dropdown.component.css']
})
export class DropdownComponent {
  @Input() placeholder = 'Select an option';
  @Input() options: { label: string; value: any }[] = [];
  @Input() selectedValue: any = null;
  @Output() selectionChange = new EventEmitter<any>();

  @ViewChild('dropdownTrigger') triggerRef!: ElementRef;
  isOpen = false;

  get displayValue(): string {
    const selectedOption = this.options.find(opt => opt.value === this.selectedValue);
    return selectedOption ? selectedOption.label : this.placeholder;
  }

  toggleDropdown(): void {
    this.isOpen = !this.isOpen;
  }

  selectOption(option: { label: string; value: any }): void {
    this.selectedValue = option.value;
    this.selectionChange.emit(option.value);
    this.isOpen = false;
  }

  @HostListener('document:click', ['$event'])
  handleClickOutside(event: Event): void {
    if (this.isOpen && !this.triggerRef.nativeElement.contains(event.target)) {
      this.isOpen = false;
    }
  }
}
```

### 2. Template (`dropdown.component.html`)
```html
<div class="dropdown" #dropdownTrigger="ngIf">
  <button 
    type="button" 
    class="dropdown-trigger" 
    [class.open]="isOpen"
    (click)="toggleDropdown()"
  >
    {{ displayValue }}
    <span class="caret"></span>
  </button>

  <ul class="dropdown-menu" *ngIf="isOpen">
    <li 
      *ngFor="let option of options" 
      class="dropdown-item"
      [class.selected]="option.value === selectedValue"
      (click)="selectOption(option)"
    >
      {{ option.label }}
    </li>
    <li *ngIf="options.length === 0" class="dropdown-empty">
      No options available
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
```

### 3. Styles (`dropdown.component.css`)
```css
.dropdown {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  min-width: 200px;
}

.dropdown-trigger {
  width: 100%;
  padding: 10px 15px;
  text-align: left;
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 4px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: border-color 0.3s;
}

.dropdown-trigger:hover {
  border-color: #888;
}

.dropdown-trigger.open {
  border-color: #007bff;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(0, 123, 255, 0.25);
}

.caret {
  float: right;
  margin-left: 10px;
  transition: transform 0.3s;
}

.dropdown-trigger.open .caret {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}

.dropdown-menu {
  position: absolute;
  top: 100%;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  margin: 5px 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  border-radius: 4px;
  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.15);
  z-index: 1000;
  max-height: 300px;
  overflow-y: auto;
}

.dropdown-item {
  padding: 10px 15px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.2s;
}

.dropdown-item:hover {
  background-color: #f5f5f5;
}

.dropdown-item.selected {
  background-color: #e6f7ff;
  font-weight: 500;
}

.dropdown-empty {
  padding: 12px;
  color: #999;
  text-align: center;
  font-style: italic;
}
```

### 4. Usage Example (`parent.component.html`)
```html
<app-dropdown
  [placeholder]="'Choose a fruit'"
  [options]="fruitOptions"
  [selectedValue]="selectedFruit"
  (selectionChange)="onFruitSelected($event)"
></app-dropdown>

<div *ngIf="selectedFruit" class="selection">
  Selected: {{ selectedFruit | json }}
</div>
```

### 5. Parent Component Logic (`parent.component.ts`)
```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-parent',
  templateUrl: './parent.component.html'
})
export class ParentComponent {
  selectedFruit: string | null = null;

  fruitOptions = [
    { label: 'Apple', value: 'apple' },
    { label: 'Banana', value: 'banana' },
    { label: 'Orange', value: 'orange' },
    { label: 'Strawberry', value: 'strawberry' }
  ];

  onFruitSelected(value: string) {
    this.selectedFruit = value;
    console.log('Selected fruit:', value);
  }
}
```

### Key Features:

1. **Type-Safe Options**: Uses structured option objects (`{ label: string, value: any }`)
2. **Two-Way Binding Support**: Works with `[(selectedValue)]` if needed
3. **Accessibility**: 
   - Proper button semantics
   - Visual feedback for selection
   - Keyboard navigation support (can be extended)
4. **User Experience**:
   - Click outside to close
   - Empty state handling
   - Visual selection indicators
   - Smooth animations
5. **Customization**:
   - Configurable placeholder
   - Works with any data type for values
   - Responsive design
6. **Error Prevention**:
   - Null safety checks
   - Empty options handling
   - Click event isolation

### How to Use:

1. Install in your project:
```bash
ng generate component dropdown
```

2. Replace the generated files with the code above

3. Import into your module:
```typescript
@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    // ...
    DropdownComponent
  ]
})
```

4. Use in any component as shown in the usage example

### Customization Options:

| Input | Type | Default | Description |
|-------|------|---------|-------------|
| `placeholder` | string | `'Select an option'` | Text when nothing selected |
| `options` | `{label: string, value: any}[]` | `[]` | Dropdown options |
| `selectedValue` | any | `null` | Currently selected value |
| `selectionChange` | EventEmitter<any> | - | Emits when selection changes |

### Advanced Features (can be added later):

1. **Keyboard Navigation**:
```typescript
@HostListener('keydown', ['$event'])
handleKeyboard(event: KeyboardEvent) {
  if (this.isOpen) {
    // Implement arrow key navigation
  }
}
```

2. **Search Filter**:
```html
<input type="text" 
       *ngIf="isOpen" 
       (input)="filterOptions($event.target.value)"
       placeholder="Search...">
```

3. **Async Support**:
```typescript
@Input() options$!: Observable<{label: string, value: any}[]>;
```

